[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Scotch Game: Scotch Gambit"]
[ECO "C44"]
[Character "sharp,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "centre-fight,transposition"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Opponent "3.d4 exd4 4.Bc4"]
[Start "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4"]

4. Bc4 { A gambit: White would rather develop than win the pawn back at once. } 4... Bc5 { Develops with a bishop that attacks f2, matching what Black plays against the Italian. } 5. c3 Nf6 { Hits e4 and makes ...dxc3 unnecessary: Black can give the pawn back or keep it, as it chooses. } 6. cxd4 { This reaches the main line of the Italian d4 line (Bishop on c4, pawns on c3 and d4 traded). One line to learn covers both openings. } ( 6. e5 d5 7. Bb5 Ne4 8. cxd4 Bb6 ) 6... Bb4+ 7. Bd2 Bxd2+ 8. Nbxd2 d5 *
